{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Threat Assessment.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Threat Assessment.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"threat assessment threat assessment","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Threat Assessment.md","fileName":"Threat Assessment.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Threat Assessment","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-09 00:00\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Cloud Security Monitoring and Resilience]] [[Cyber Threat Vulnerability and Risk Analysis]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cloud Security Monitoring and Resilience","Cyber Threat Vulnerability and Risk Analysis","Security Risk","Cyber Threat","Cyber Vulnerability","cloudcomputing_mit.epub","cybersecurity.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Threat Assessment.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Threat Assessment.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"threat assessment threat assessment","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Threat Assessment.md","fileName":"Threat Assessment.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Threat Assessment","heading":"Threat Assessment","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A threat assessment identifies the kinds of harmful events, actors, or conditions to which an organization and its information may be exposed. It considers attacks from outside, misuse from inside, compromised clients, interrupted providers, and failures along the data journey.\n\nThe result informs [[Security Risk]] and the selection of preventive, detective, and recovery controls. Threats should be reassessed when a cloud deployment changes its users, locations, service providers, interfaces, or stored data.\n\nA cybersecurity assessment begins by identifying valuable information assets, then enumerates [[Cyber Threat|threats]] and [[Cyber Vulnerability|vulnerabilities]] that could